# Optional credentials for squad. ALL of this is optional: with no keys at all the loop still runs
# (Trello sync is skipped, and @developer/@qa use the Agent tool fallback).
#
#   cp .env.example ~/.claude/squad.env   ← then fill it in there
#
# It lives in ~/.claude/ on purpose: installed as a plugin, this repo sits in a cache directory
# that is replaced on every update, so a .env kept in here would be lost. Shell variables always
# win over this file.
#
# --- Trello: BOARD mirror (/squad:board and the close of /squad:run) ---
#
# Where they come from: https://trello.com/power-ups/admin → your power-up → API key tab.
# CAREFUL: that page shows an "API Key" and a "Secret". THE SECRET DOES NOT GO HERE (it is for
# OAuth and this script never uses it). What goes here is:
#   TRELLO_KEY   = the API Key.
#   TRELLO_TOKEN = the TOKEN generated from the "Token" link next to the key (you authorize by
#                  hand and it gives you a long string).
TRELLO_KEY=
TRELLO_TOKEN=

# --- OpenRouter: engine for @developer and @qa (see /squad:run §OpenRouter engine) ---
#
# Key: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys — without it the loop uses the fallback (Agent tool)
# and carries on.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to openai/gpt-5.6-sol:
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=
